{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_3>\ndef compute_sl():\n    sl = [0] * 51\n    sl[0] = 1\n    for i in range(1, 51):\n        sl[i] = sl[i-1] + (2 << i-1)\n    return sl\n\nsl = compute_sl()\n\nh, n = map(int, input().split())\n\ndef build_path(target):\n    path = [target]\n    while target != 1:\n        target //= 2\n        path.append(target)\n    return path\n\nadjusted_n = n + sl[h-1]\nnl = build_path(adjusted_n)\n\nans = 0\ncn = 1\ncp = False\n\nwhile cn != adjusted_n:\n    tnl = []\n    for _ in range(h):\n        tnl.append(cn)\n        cn = (cn << 1) if not cp else (cn << 1) + 1\n        cp = not cp\n    if cn == adjusted_n:\n        ans += h\n        break\n    \n    tnl.append(cn)\n    tnl = list(reversed(tnl))\n    for i in range(1, h+1):\n        if nl[i] == tnl[i]:\n            ans += sl[i-1] + h - i + 1\n            h = i - 1\n            cn = tnl[i-1]\n            if cn == (tnl[i] << 1):\n                cn = (tnl[i] << 1) + 1\n                cp = False\n            else:\n                cn = tnl[i] << 1\n                cp = True\n            break\nprint(ans)\n</your_rewritten_code_3>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nvector<long long> compute_sl() {\n    vector<long long> sl(51, 0);\n    sl[0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= 50; i++) {\n        sl[i] = sl[i-1] + (2LL << (i-1));\n    }\n    return sl;\n}\n\nvector<long long> build_path(long long target) {\n    vector<long long> path;\n    path.push_back(target);\n    while (target != 1) {\n        target /= 2;\n        path.push_back(target);\n    }\n    return path;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    vector<long long> sl = compute_sl();\n    \n    long long h, n;\n    cin >> h >> n;\n    \n    long long adjusted_n = n + sl[h-1];\n    vector<long long> nl = build_path(adjusted_n);\n    \n    long long ans = 0;\n    long long cn = 1;\n    bool cp = false;\n    \n    while (cn != adjusted_n) {\n        vector<long long> tnl;\n        for (int _ = 0; _ < h; _++) {\n            tnl.push_back(cn);\n            if (!cp) {\n                cn = cn << 1;\n            } else {\n                cn = (cn << 1) + 1;\n            }\n            cp = !cp;\n        }\n        if (cn == adjusted_n) {\n            ans += h;\n            break;\n        }\n        \n        tnl.push_back(cn);\n        reverse(tnl.begin(), tnl.end());\n        for (int i = 1; i <= h; i++) {\n            if (nl[i] == tnl[i]) {\n                ans += sl[i-1] + h - i + 1;\n                h = i - 1;\n                cn = tnl[i-1];\n                if (cn == (tnl[i] << 1)) {\n                    cn = (tnl[i] << 1) + 1;\n                    cp = false;\n                } else {\n                    cn = tnl[i] << 1;\n                    cp = true;\n                }\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << ans << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>"